---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
// The Download page: the latest release's installer, as its update file names it (scripts/sync.mjs), with its size and
// SHA-256 and the line that checks it; or, while there is no release, how to build Phazite. Then the other systems,
// Phazite Sounds and the source.
import { Aside, Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import LucideIcon from '../components/LucideIcon.astro';
import { formatSize, getRelease, repository, withBase } from '../lib/site';

const release = getRelease();
const check = release ? `(Get-FileHash .\\${release.fileName}).Hash -eq '${release.sha256}'` : '';
---

<StarlightPage
	frontmatter={{
		title: 'Download',
		description: release
			? `Phazite ${release.version} for Windows: the installer, its SHA-256, and what's next for Linux and macOS.`
			: "Phazite has no release yet: how to build it yourself on Windows, and what's next for Linux and macOS.",
		editUrl: `https://github.com/august-byrne/phazite-site/edit/main/src/pages/download.astro`,
		tableOfContents: false,
	}}
>
	{
		release ? (
			<>
				<div class="get pz-card not-content">
					<div>
						<p class="name">Phazite {release.version} for Windows</p>
						<p class="details">Windows 11 x64 · {formatSize(release.size)} · installs for you, without admin rights</p>
					</div>
					<a class="pz-button primary" href={release.installer}>
						<LucideIcon name="download" />
						Download the installer
					</a>
				</div>
				<Aside type="caution" title="Pre-alpha">
					Phazite changes from one build to the next, and projects saved now may not open in later builds. Export what
					you want to keep as audio.
				</Aside>
				<p>
					<a href={release.notes}>What's new in {release.version}</a> · <a href={`${repository}/releases`}>All releases</a>
				</p>

				<h2>Check the download</h2>
				<p>
					In PowerShell, in the folder you downloaded it to, this prints <code>True</code> when the installer is the one
					the release was built with:
				</p>
				<Code code={check} lang="powershell" />

				<h2>Install and update</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						The installer puts Phazite in your user folder without asking for admin rights. Run it with{' '}
						<code>/ALLUSERS</code> to install for every user of the PC instead.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Help > Check for Updates...</strong> finds a newer version, and installs it when you say so. To check
						each time Phazite opens, turn on <strong>Check for Updates When Phazite Opens</strong>.
					</li>
					<li>
						Windows' <strong>Installed apps</strong> removes Phazite and leaves your projects, presets, sounds and
						settings.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</>
		) : (
			<>
				<p>
					Phazite is pre-alpha and has no release yet. Until the first one, you build it yourself, on Windows 11 x64 with
					about 15 GB free: the README's <a href={`${repository}#try-it`}>Try it</a> has the steps, and{' '}
					<a href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/building.md`}>Building Phazite</a> explains each one, with fixes for
					when something goes wrong. The build takes a few minutes once its tools are set up.
				</p>
				<div class="get pz-card not-content">
					<div>
						<p class="name">Phazite on Windows 11 x64</p>
						<p class="details">Pre-alpha · built from its source code</p>
					</div>
					<a class="pz-button primary" href={`${repository}#try-it`}>
						How to build it
					</a>
				</div>
				<Aside title="Hear when it's out">
					On GitHub, <strong>Watch</strong> Phazite's repository and choose <strong>Custom</strong> and{' '}
					<strong>Releases</strong> to hear when the first installer is out.
				</Aside>
			</>
		)
	}

	<h2>Other systems</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Linux</strong> builds and passes its tests, and a beta comes with the first releases. Until then, <a
				href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/building.md`}>build it from its source code</a>.
		</li>
		<li><strong>macOS</strong> comes after version 1, with Audio Units.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Phazite Sounds</h2>
	<p>
		85 drums, loops and effects, free and in the public domain (CC0). The Welcome window downloads them when you ask, and
		so does <strong>Help > Phazite Sounds</strong>. They are made in <a href="https://github.com/august-byrne/phazite-sounds"
			>their own repository</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>Source code</h2>
	<p>
		Phazite's code is on <a href={repository}>GitHub</a>, under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later.
		Each release's code is its tag there. <a href={withBase('guide/getting-started/')}>Getting started</a> shows what to do
		first.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.get {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		margin-block: 1.5rem;
		padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.get p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.name {
		color: var(--pz-text-bright);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.details {
		margin-top: 0.25rem !important;
		color: var(--pz-text-muted);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
</style>
